ur straight.\n\nReason:  \nChecking preserves chips and maintains pressure on the opponent who has shown weakness. It allows you to see the river without committing more chips. A raise risks getting raised off your hand and losing more when behind. With no prior aggression, a bluff is less likely to succeed against even a weak calling range.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
